# Proofread before push

Before every `git push` of this site, check all user-facing English in the change (About, posts, category labels, nav, meta descriptions). Fix spelling and grammar. Do not wait for the user to notice.

Keep the site voice: mostly lowercase, short sentences, no marketing phrasing. Fix errors; do not rewrite their wording unless it is wrong.

```text
❌ Constistency matters more than intensity
✅ Consistency matters more than intensity

❌ reasearch
✅ research
```

After copy fixes, proofread, then commit source and push. A GitHub Action rebuilds `docs/` on `main`. Do not commit `.cursor/skills/`. Run `npm run build` locally only when you need to check the static output yourself.
